t promos  and we'll tell it to automatically  detect the schema and just like that  within a few moments there we will have  a table created for us locally  this would be a table that the yankees  have access to that otherwise is not  shared anywhere else  now uh the join could be written that  combines those two things together so  i've  written this query up here that says  let's take the data that major league  baseball would have shared with us in  the tickets data set  and we're going to do a join with the  promos data on the game date  and this will allow us to run that query  that crosses those two data sets and  sees which promotion has the highest  overall quantity sold  so in this example here we see that the  highest quantity sold was a t-shirt  that led to the most quantity sold other  than no promotions which were there  because perhaps  we didn't fill in all the promo data so  you can see how this paradigm of being  able to join across data sets you're  authorized to  allows you to have different access  patterns for data  while still allowing centralized  querying across them thanks rob and  thank you for joining us for google  cloud next be sure to check out some of  our other great data analytics sessions  thank you  you
 

